WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.335 --> 00:00:15.136
to rescue the young widow would be a bold undertaking, maybe even an impossible one.

2
00:00:16.496 --> 00:00:16.996
But Mr.

3
00:00:17.036 --> 00:00:20.877
Fogg did not hesitate, and Sir Francis was an enthusiastic ally.

4
00:00:22.258 --> 00:00:26.199
Passepartout was ready for anything, and even the guide was on their side.

5
00:00:26.219 --> 00:00:28.820
"Where are they taking her?"

6
00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:29.760
asked Mr.

7
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:34.783
Fogg. "To the pagoda of Pillaji, two miles from here," said the guide.

8
00:00:34.803 --> 00:00:40.667
"The woman will spend the night there, and the sacrifice will take place at the first light of

9
00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:43.949
dawn." The guide looked at the group of rescuers.

10
00:00:43.969 --> 00:00:51.334
"It is certain that we shall risk not only our lives but horrible tortures if we are caught!"

11
00:00:51.354 --> 00:00:54.757
"That is foreseen," said Mr.

12
00:00:54.797 --> 00:00:59.120
Fogg. "I think we must wait until night before acting."

13
00:01:00.592 --> 00:01:02.654
"I agree," said Sir Francis.

14
00:01:03.615 --> 00:01:05.476
Their guide gave an account of the woman.

15
00:01:05.496 --> 00:01:11.942
"She is the daughter of a wealthy Bombay merchant and received an excellent English education.

16
00:01:13.363 --> 00:01:14.644
Her name is Aouda.

17
00:01:15.965 --> 00:01:20.889
While still very young, she was left an orphan and was married against her will to an old

18
00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.994
rajah. When he died, she escaped, knowing the fate that awaited her.

19
00:01:27.315 --> 00:01:28.356
But she was captured.

20
00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:31.682
That is why she is under such heavy guard now."

21
00:01:32.942 --> 00:01:35.684
The guide's story strengthened the determination of Mr.

22
00:01:35.724 --> 00:01:36.624
Fogg and his friends.

23
00:01:38.846 --> 00:01:42.488
As soon as night fell, the guide led them deeper into the thick jungle.

24
00:01:44.089 --> 00:01:45.930
They came to an area lit by torches.

25
00:01:46.810 --> 00:01:51.593
A group of Indians were sleeping outside a wide brick wall that enclosed the tall pagoda.

26
00:01:52.854 --> 00:01:55.896
Guards with swords marched back and forth before the doors.

27
00:01:57.556 --> 00:02:01.158
The rescuers hid themselves and waited, hoping the guards would fall asleep.

28
00:02:02.599 --> 00:02:06.862
After midnight, when it was clear that the guards were going to patrol all night, Fogg and his

29
00:02:06.922 --> 00:02:09.704
companions sneaked around to the back of the pagoda.

30
00:02:10.804 --> 00:02:13.766
With two sturdy knives that their guide had brought, Mr.

31
00:02:13.806 --> 00:02:17.589
Fogg and Sir Francis worked quietly at the loose bricks of the wall.

32
00:02:18.469 --> 00:02:22.752
They managed to dislodge a few and then found they could remove the other bricks with their hands.

33
00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:27.843
Their plan was to open a hole large enough for Aouda to slip through.

34
00:02:29.124 --> 00:02:31.526
Suddenly a cry arose from inside the pagoda.

35
00:02:32.907 --> 00:02:36.990
Mr. Fogg and his friends escaped into the jungle just as the guards ran to the back of

36
00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:37.551
the pagoda.

37
00:02:39.112 --> 00:02:44.376
Sir Francis shook his fists, Passepartout was furious, and the guide grimaced with rage.

38
00:02:45.737 --> 00:02:47.158
How could they save Aouda now?

39
00:02:47.659 --> 00:02:48.519
The tranquil Mr.

40
00:02:48.559 --> 00:02:50.601
Fogg waited, revealing no emotion.

41
00:02:50.621 --> 00:02:55.569
"We can do nothing but go on our way," whispered Sir Francis.

42
00:02:55.589 --> 00:02:57.410
"He is right.

43
00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.490
We must go," said the guide.

44
00:02:59.511 --> 00:03:02.012
"Stop," said Fogg.

45
00:03:02.032 --> 00:03:05.553
"I am not due at Allahabad before noon tomorrow.

46
00:03:06.754 --> 00:03:08.755
We may get another chance to rescue her."

47
00:03:08.775 --> 00:03:12.176
"What is this cool Englishman thinking?"

48
00:03:12.557 --> 00:03:13.597
Sir Francis wondered.

49
00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:19.360
"Is he planning to boldly snatch the woman from her executioners at the very moment of the sacrifice?"

50
00:03:21.064 --> 00:03:25.226
It was hard to believe that the calm Phileas Fogg could attempt something so desperate.

51
00:03:26.507 --> 00:03:30.248
They crept around the outskirts of the clearing and made their way back to the doors of the

52
00:03:30.288 --> 00:03:36.431
pagoda. Concealed by the jungle, Fogg and his companions watched through the night.

53
00:03:38.032 --> 00:03:40.213
Passepartout climbed into the branches of a tree.

54
00:03:41.573 --> 00:03:46.235
While he was perched there, an idea struck him, and the more he considered it, the more firmly

55
00:03:46.295 --> 00:03:47.276
it lodged in his brain.

56
00:03:48.972 --> 00:03:54.056
The lengthening shadows announced the approach of day, and the Indians sleeping outside the pagoda woke up.

57
00:03:55.517 --> 00:03:57.498
Tambourines sounded and chanting began.

58
00:03:58.719 --> 00:04:00.440
The hour of the sacrifice had come.

59
00:04:01.881 --> 00:04:03.682
The doors of the pagoda swung open.

60
00:04:03.702 --> 00:04:08.345
Aouda was led out, struggling in the clutches of two large guards.

61
00:04:09.546 --> 00:04:12.128
Sir Francis' heart throbbed, and he seized Mr.

62
00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:12.868
Fogg's hand.

63
00:04:14.269 --> 00:04:15.911
He was surprised to discover that Mr.

64
00:04:15.951 --> 00:04:17.692
Fogg's hand gripped a knife tightly.

65
00:04:19.281 --> 00:04:24.225
Phileas Fogg and his companions mingled at the back of the crowd as the funeral procession made its

66
00:04:24.285 --> 00:04:25.126
way to a stream.

67
00:04:26.287 --> 00:04:30.651
On the bank of the stream, the body of the rajah who had been Aouda's husband lay on

68
00:04:30.691 --> 00:04:32.772
a large pile of carefully stacked wood.

69
00:04:34.134 --> 00:04:35.575
From the back of the crowd, Mr.

70
00:04:35.635 --> 00:04:36.736
Fogg saw Aouda.

71
00:04:38.117 --> 00:04:42.201
She was lying senseless beside her dead husband at the top of the funeral pyre.

72
00:04:43.702 --> 00:04:45.504
The Brahmin leader brought a torch.

73
00:04:46.476 --> 00:04:49.779
The wood was heavily soaked in oil and instantly caught on fire.

74
00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:56.344
Phileas Fogg let out a desperate moan, and Sir Francis and the guide seized him before he could

75
00:04:56.424 --> 00:04:58.106
rush onto the climbing flames.

76
00:04:59.707 --> 00:05:02.169
He pushed them aside and stepped to the front of the crowd.

77
00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.652
Just then a cry of terror arose.

78
00:05:06.853 --> 00:05:08.274
The old rajah was not dead!

79
00:05:09.616 --> 00:05:14.560
He stood, took his wife in his arms, and, amidst a cloud of smoke, descended from the pyre.

80
00:05:15.860 --> 00:05:18.082
Mr. Fogg and Sir Francis stood in shock.

81
00:05:19.564 --> 00:05:23.527
The guide bowed his head, and all the Brahmins kneeled with their faces to the ground.

82
00:05:25.369 --> 00:05:25.789
To Mr.

83
00:05:25.829 --> 00:05:30.193
Fogg's amazement, the rajah who had returned from the dead walked directly up to him.

84
00:05:30.213 --> 00:05:32.715
"Let us be off!"

85
00:05:33.136 --> 00:05:33.576
he said.

86
00:05:34.617 --> 00:05:37.600
But it wasn't the rajah at all—it was Passepartout!

87
00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:42.324
Ha! Were you surprised?

88
00:05:43.636 --> 00:05:46.297
If my plan had failed, I wouldn't be here talking to you now!

89
00:05:47.518 --> 00:05:49.919
Cremation of the dead is very common in Hinduism.

90
00:05:50.959 --> 00:05:55.841
A large funeral pyre is built, usually alongside a river, and the body of the deceased is placed

91
00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:56.261
on top.

92
00:05:57.502 --> 00:06:01.343
With the help of a priest, the eldest son of the deceased will then light the fire.

93
00:06:02.944 --> 00:06:05.665
After the cremation the deceased's soul is said to be naked.

94
00:06:06.986 --> 00:06:12.208
Family members must perform various rites and ceremonies to provide the deceased with a "new spiritual body."

95
00:06:13.277 --> 00:06:17.615
Eventually the bones of the deceased are collected and then either buried or placed into a river.
